    spyRounds: [
      { crewmateTopic:"Embedded Questions", spyTopic:"Direct Questions", crewmatePrompt:"Ask about your partner's daily routine, plans, and opinions — but use polite embedded forms: 'Could you tell me...', 'Do you know...', 'I'd like to know...', 'I wonder if...'", spyPrompt:"Ask about daily routine, plans, and opinions using direct questions: 'What do you do in the morning?', 'When do you finish work?', 'Do you have any plans this weekend?'", explanation:"Crewmates use embedded questions with statement word order (no inversion). The spy uses direct questions with standard question word order." },
      { crewmateTopic:"Embedded Questions (asking for information)", spyTopic:"Indirect Speech (Reported Questions)", crewmatePrompt:"Ask for directions and information in the street — use embedded questions: 'Excuse me, do you know where the museum is?', 'Could you tell me if the bus stops here?'", spyPrompt:"Report questions that someone asked you — 'She asked me where the museum was', 'He wanted to know if the bus stopped there', 'They asked me whether I knew the way'.", explanation:"Crewmates use embedded questions to politely ask for information. The spy reports what was asked (past tense, backshifted)." },
      { crewmateTopic:"Embedded Questions (uncertainty)", spyTopic:"Question Tags", crewmatePrompt:"Express uncertainty about various topics — 'I'm not sure if he's coming', 'I wonder whether the café is open', 'Do you have any idea what time it closes?'", spyPrompt:"Check information using question tags — 'He's coming, isn't he?', 'The café is open, isn't it?', 'It closes at six, doesn't it?'", explanation:"Crewmates use embedded questions to express uncertainty (statement word order). The spy uses question tags to confirm information." },
      { crewmateTopic:"Embedded Questions (not knowing)", spyTopic:"Nominal Clauses (know/think/believe + that)", crewmatePrompt:"Talk about what you're unsure of using embedded questions — 'I'm not sure what the answer is', 'I wonder if they'll agree', 'I have no idea where she went'.", spyPrompt:"Talk about things you're sure about, using 'I think that', 'I believe that', 'I know that', or 'I'm sure that' — expressing certainty.", explanation:"Crewmates use embedded questions for things they don't know (uncertainty). The spy uses nominal 'that-clauses' to express what they do know or believe." },
    ],
